diff --git a/docs/next/website/src/content/docs/agent-automation.mdx b/docs/next/website/src/content/docs/agent-automation.mdx
index def306fabcaa7a99d4d00804bd89d51a0f61fca7..748d7456411b0ae7a047d7e63bcd4158ba1fd3cf 100644
--- a/docs/next/website/src/content/docs/agent-automation.mdx
+++ b/docs/next/website/src/content/docs/agent-automation.mdx
@@ -81,6 +81,17 @@ Startup readiness, restoring an idle conversation, and switching agent conversat
 
 A timeout or `agent_prompt_stalled` does not prove that no input was sent. Read the agent before retrying to avoid submitting the same prompt twice. IDs and agent names are scoped to one server; selecting another machine in the TUI does not retarget CLI commands running in an existing pane.
 
+### Guarded original-terminal submission (API)
+
+An integration that requires an original spawn must use a source build supporting guarded prompts and require `guarded_prompt: true` plus `guarded_prompt_origin` from `pane.process-info`. This capability is available only for an attached Linux terminal whose original child was captured with a live pidfd. Imported or handed-off terminals and unsupported capture do not advertise it. Select and authenticate the intended server/build before reading its capability; an older server's ordinary prompt acknowledgment is not guarded evidence.
+
+Call `agent.prompt` with `target` equal to that exact opaque `terminal_id`, `text`, and the complete `expected_origin` object unchanged. The object contains `terminal_id`, `runtime_incarnation`, and `child` (`pid`, `uid`, `gid`, `groups`, `parent_pid`, `started_at`, `host`). Unknown fields, aliases, malformed identities, `wait`, blank text, and text above 16384 UTF-8 bytes are refused. Guarded calls do not use pane names or agent labels.
+
+The original child and runtime must still match when admitted and immediately before each focus/text/Enter write to the captured PTY. A complete acknowledgment contains `submission: "submitted"` and the exact `origin`; it proves ordered terminal submission, not agent consumption. Refusals report `error.phase: "not_issued"` when no guarded input was written. Partial writes, write errors, or uncertain completion report `"issued_or_unknown"`. A lost acknowledgment is also uncertain. Never automatically resend an uncertain prompt. The same original terminal may deliver to its foreground descendant; this protocol does not authenticate which descendant consumed the text.
+
+Queued guarded submissions prevent PTY handoff until completed or refused. Replacement or original-child exit before the first write has no focus/text effect. Exit after partial input suppresses further text/Enter and remains uncertain. Protected stop and whole-scope writer/settlement proofs belong to the external canonical owner; guarded prompt acknowledgment does not authorize cleanup.
+
+
 `pane wait-output` does not interpret agent lifecycle. It polls the selected terminal snapshot and searches it immediately, so text that was already present can match. The default source name is `recent`; matching treats that source as unwrapped recent output from the latest 80 rendered terminal rows. `--lines` changes that row limit, and `--regex` uses Rust regular-expression syntax and matches one line at a time.
 
 At the CLI, both `pane read` and `agent read` print terminal text directly. The default is UTF-8 text with ANSI escapes stripped; use `--format ansi` or `--ansi` to preserve terminal escapes where the source exposes them. The `detection` source is always plain text. For recent sources, `--lines N` selects the last N rendered terminal rows before optional unwrapping; without it, reads default to 80 rows. For `visible` and `detection`, omitting `--lines` returns the full snapshot, while specifying it keeps the last N newline-delimited lines. The socket API returns the text at `.result.read.text`.
